{
  "_what": "Layer 4 of the four-layer derivation: the component catalogues of the three public-service design systems we hold ourselves to. Captured as DATA so provenance is matched, not decided — the same shape as openui-names.json for layer 3.",
  "_why": "Layer 4 used to be a hand-written table of 11 entries inside derive-provenance.mjs. A gate whose reference is a list somebody typed measures that list: eleven recipes could have a layer-4 source and no twelfth ever would, because nobody would think to add it. The cut list — the thing anyone will actually act on — was therefore too long by however many components these systems ship that we had not happened to notice.",
  "_honesty": "This is a CAPTURED SNAPSHOT of published component indexes, not a live fetch, so it can go stale exactly like openui-names.json. Every entry carries the system's own component name and a URL, so any single claim is checkable in one click — which is the property that matters. Where a name here turns out to be wrong, the fix is to correct the entry, never to loosen the matcher.",
